-- Genuine loops, each used by two directives. Giving a raised thunk its mark
-- back must not turn the loop check off: every use is still reported as an
-- infinite loop. (A definition that is its own operand, and a pair that are
-- each other's.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`self loop` MEANS `self loop` PLUS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`ping` MEANS `pong` PLUS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`pong` MEANS `ping` PLUS 1

#EVAL `self loop`
#EVAL `self loop`
#EVAL `ping`
#EVAL `ping`
